#: ../../study/methodology.md:201
msgid ""
"This trend cap is not a physical constraint of the system but a budgetary"
" assumption: the share of transmission investment of each country is "
"calibrated from the distribution of the investment observed in 163 "
"BNAmericas projects in operation and under construction, checked against "
"the tracking of the expansion plans of the national regulators. That "
"distribution portrays today's committed portfolio and does not measure "
"the grid needs to 2050. Keeping that cap rigid over the whole horizon is "
"equivalent to projecting the current pace of investment, including the "
"documented underinvestment of several systems, as if that pace were the "
"maximum delivery capacity of the country."
msgstr ""
"Este tope tendencial no es una restricción física del sistema, sino un "
"supuesto presupuestario: la cuota de inversión en transmisión de cada "
"país se calibra a partir del reparto de la inversión observada en 163 "
"proyectos de BNAmericas en operación y construcción, contrastado con el "
"rastreo de los planes de expansión de los reguladores nacionales. Ese "
"reparto retrata la cartera comprometida hoy y no mide la necesidad de red"
" al 2050. Mantener ese tope rígido durante todo el horizonte equivale a "
"proyectar el ritmo de inversión actual incluida la subinversión "
"documentada de varios sistemas como si ese ritmo fuera la capacidad "
"máxima de entrega del país."

#: ../../study/methodology.md:203
msgid ""
"Kilometres of lines by type: length of transmission lines distinguished "
"between planned, repowered and new unplanned lines (km)."
msgstr ""
"Kilómetros de líneas por tipo: longitud de líneas de transmisión "
"diferenciada entre planificadas, repotenciadas y nuevas no planificadas "
"(km)."

#: ../../study/methodology.md:205
msgid ""
"Fuels ×1.70: High Oil Price case of the EIA AEO2025: Brent reaches 155 "
"USD/b in 2050 compared with 91 USD/b in the Reference case; ratio = 1.7. "
"Fuels ×0.52: Low Oil Price case of the EIA AEO2025: Brent stands at 47 "
"USD/b in 2050 compared with 91 USD/b in the Reference case; ratio = 0.52."
" Solar PV ×1.33: Conservative Technology Innovation scenario of the NREL "
"ATB 2024, Utility-Scale PV, Class 5: CAPEX (overnight cost plus grid "
"connection) is 1,148 USD/kW_AC in 2035 compared with 864 USD/kW_AC in the"
" Moderate scenario (2022 USD); ratio = 1.33. Solar PV ×0.60: Moderate "
"Technology Innovation scenario of the NREL ATB 2024, Utility-Scale PV, "
"Class 5: CAPEX (overnight cost plus grid connection) falls to 864 "
"USD/kW_AC in 2035 compared with 1,431 USD/kW_AC in 2022 (2022 USD); ratio"
" = 0.60. Storage ×1.49: Conservative scenario of the NREL ATB 2024, "
"Utility-Scale Battery Storage, 4Hr: CAPEX is 1,492 USD/kW in 2050 "
"compared with 999 USD/kW in the Moderate scenario (2022 USD); ratio = "
"1.49. Storage ×0.50: Moderate scenario of the NREL ATB 2024, Utility-"
"Scale Battery Storage, 4Hr: CAPEX falls to 999 USD/kW in 2050 compared "
"with 2,027 USD/kW in 2022 (2022 USD); ratio = 0.50. Onshore wind ×1.17: "
"Conservative scenario of the NREL ATB 2024, Land-Based Wind, Class 4: "
"CAPEX is 1,488 USD/kW in 2030 and 1,280 USD/kW in 2050 compared with "
"1,328 and 1,052 USD/kW in the Moderate scenario (2022 USD); mean "
"2030–2050 of the five-year Conservative/Moderate ratios (1.120; 1.140; "
"1.163; 1.188; 1.217) = 1.17. Onshore wind ×0.75: Moderate scenario of the"
" NREL ATB 2024, Land-Based Wind, Class 4: CAPEX falls from 1,572 USD/kW "
